  "2026-07-27T19:43:35.763Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence for PR #777 head preparation: CodeRabbit findings were addressed by rebuilding before generated drift checks, preserving schema properties named description while stripping annotations, moving tool-call authorization to a fast single-tool access path, honoring anyOf/oneOf conditional requirements, preserving backward-compatible optional WorkspaceContracts fields, scoping parameter descriptions by action, and cleaning generator test temp roots. Greptile reserved-field collision is impossible by contract because both runtime field registration paths reject built-in names. Verification passed: lint/ESLint, zero jscpd clones, strict 100% docstrings/static quality, typecheck/type tests/packages/examples, contract and SDK snapshots, pm-changelog 2026.7.27 check, fresh 88-operation package-first dogfood, Claude MCP smoke, packed npx smoke, and focused PM-linked 12-test suite. Authoritative direct coverage: 379 files, 6,428 tests, 100% statements (44,600/44,600), branches (31,718/31,718), functions (9,138/9,138), and lines (43,317/43,317). Two intentionally recorded linked coverage attempts showed PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT changes file-governance semantics; the distinct dedupe-checked UX gap is pm-efkvdy, so the recursive whole-repo test was removed from this item and replaced with safe focused linked regressions."
  "2026-07-27T20:14:29.395Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review follow-up: CodeRabbit correctly identified that the shared text parameter description did not describe close and close-task. Added action-scoped close-reason descriptions, regenerated the full public contract fixture, added runtime schema regressions, up-voted and replied inline with evidence, and resolved the thread. Verification passed: focused runtime-capability tests, contracts drift check, full lint/static/docstring/zero-duplication gates, and authoritative coverage across 379 files and 6,428 tests at 100% statements (44,600/44,600), branches (31,718/31,718), functions (9,138/9,138), and lines (43,317/43,317)."
